      "side": 1,
      "message": "SessionHandlerConfigurator overrides the ServerKeyVerifier and the auth factories after clientParams is applied, so server-authentication and the client-identity auth methods in clientParams are silently ignored here (and a configured password, I believe, stays on the client as a fallback for every device). Could this overload reject such clientParams, or take only transport params and keepalives, so the \"ignored\" username in call-home can go too?",
