      "writtenOn": "2026-10-22T14:37:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sshd calls the ServerKeyVerifier again on every key re-exchange (by default hourly), so checkServerKey also runs for an authenticated session, despite the Javadoc saying \"before authentication\". Call-home then hits contextManager.exists() and drops its own device. Could we remember the accepted key in a session attribute and, on re-key, just compare it with KeyUtils.compareKeys without calling the handler, plus a reExchangeKeys() test?",
